# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in every working tree.
#
# This repository is edited on Windows and run on Linux in three places: the
# Netlify build and its Node functions, the GitHub Actions runner, and the Deno
# edge runtime that will load src/lib/core/** unchanged under AD-2. A file that
# picks up CRLF on the way through a Windows checkout is a file whose diff
# depends on who committed it.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is what introduces that: it writes CRLF into working
# copies on checkout. Every tracked file is already LF in the index, so this
# file changes no repository content — it settles the working tree and keeps
# future commits from drifting.
#
# Git decides text vs binary by content, so `text=auto` leaves genuinely binary
# files alone without needing them enumerated here.

* text=auto eol=lf
